From 7c14daa7a92487ad47a11aea7369287e1ad738ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:01:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] :new: Import deferred memory without host pointers

A device without external host-memory import needs the backing files of
idle and deferred views to reach the runtime through DMA-BUF. Select the
route from the actual device's enabled extensions and pair the existing
gather source with the DMA-BUF source so the runtime can materialize the
whole window before exporting it. Keep the existing gather-only route
where the host extension is enabled.

For a deferred read-only source on that route, reuse the existing writable
twin of its files. Preserve the original address, protections, deferred
mapping state and deallocator argument, and retain the existing write
guards and import lifetime. Other platforms retain their import behavior.

Add CPU regressions for the read-only twin, the unchanged host-extension
route and writable views under both policies, including shared bytes,
page offsets and lifetime. All three pass against the combined candidate
runtime ffda2ffd. Its Android C-facade metadata check also passes through
explicit Cargo patch paths; repository dependency pins stay unchanged.
The wider native selection retains three existing failures where this
container refuses process_vm_readv on itself with EPERM. Two existing
device-backed tests pass with lavapipe. No phone or guest boot was run.
